1
00:00:00,654 --> 00:00:07,285
This is Broker Order Desk: an order desk for a stock brokerage,
with a React dashboard on a Spring Boot backend, written in Java

2
00:00:07,285 --> 00:00:13,916
twenty five. There are four roles: investor, liquidity provider,
risk officer, and administrator. Every name, symbol and price is

3
00:00:13,916 --> 00:00:17,231
synthetic.

4
00:00:18,677 --> 00:00:26,080
Investor two signs in and lands on the price board: best offer
and bid from the live order book, last price, trades, average,

5
00:00:26,080 --> 00:00:33,482
volume, value, high, low, a trend line, and the change. Ten
symbols carry synthetic opening trades.

6
00:00:34,086 --> 00:00:40,450
Investor two sells twenty thousand shares at twelve riyals and
five hundred mills. Pre trade risk reserves those shares, so

7
00:00:40,450 --> 00:00:46,813
they cannot be sold twice, and the order rests in the book. The
depth panel shows it.

8
00:00:49,144 --> 00:00:56,952
Investor one buys the same size. The engine matches by price and
time, and the trade settles in one database transaction. At the

9
00:00:56,952 --> 00:01:04,760
top, the balance turned negative: that is the margin loan. The
margin check is healthy at forty percent.

10
00:01:07,090 --> 00:01:12,829
Now the price moves. Investor two offers five thousand shares at
eleven riyals three hundred, still inside the ten percent daily

11
00:01:12,829 --> 00:01:15,699
band.

12
00:01:18,021 --> 00:01:24,118
Investor one buys a thousand at that price. The last price
drops, the position is marked to market, and equity falls below

13
00:01:24,118 --> 00:01:30,216
the maintenance level. The flag at the top turns red: margin
call.

14
00:01:30,818 --> 00:01:36,589
The margin screen shows it on a gauge: the needle is inside the
red zone, under the maintenance line.

15
00:01:38,920 --> 00:01:46,108
A risk officer signs in. Only that role sees margin calls across
accounts, and investor one is on the list.

16
00:01:48,439 --> 00:01:56,395
Back as investor one, three pre trade checks. The ticket warns
before sending, and the server still decides. A price outside

17
00:01:56,395 --> 00:02:04,351
the daily band is rejected. An order bigger than the buying
power is rejected. Selling shares you do not own is rejected.

18
00:02:06,669 --> 00:02:14,285
Investor two cancels the order that is still resting. The engine
removes it from the book and the reserved shares are released.

19
00:02:16,587 --> 00:02:22,767
The liquidity provider posts a two sided quote, a bid and an
offer together. It goes through the same risk, matching and

20
00:02:22,767 --> 00:02:25,857
settlement path as any other order.

21
00:02:28,169 --> 00:02:34,070
Finally the administrator reviews the audit trail: every
accepted order, fill, rejection and cancel, with who did it and

22
00:02:34,070 --> 00:02:37,020
a correlation id.

23
00:02:37,625 --> 00:02:44,139
Twenty seven automated tests stand behind this, including a
stress test with many concurrent orders that proves cash and

24
00:02:44,139 --> 00:02:50,652
shares are conserved, and a test where the database fails in the
middle of settlement and the desk recovers. There is a

25
00:02:50,652 --> 00:02:57,166
Dockerfile, Kubernetes manifests, a CI pipeline, specs and a
changelog for every feature, and the code is in the Git

26
00:02:57,166 --> 00:03:00,423
repository.
